---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../../components/Hero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy policy of the Pétanque Scan app | Ludiven Studio"
	description="Privacy policy of the Pétanque Scan mobile app: data processed, advertising, analytics, GDPR rights."
	lang="en"
	alternates={{ fr: '/petanque-scanner/confidentialite/', en: '/en/petanque-scanner/confidentialite/', es: '/es/petanque-scanner/confidentialite/', de: '/de/petanque-scanner/confidentialite/', it: '/it/petanque-scanner/confidentialite/' }}
>
	<div class="wrapper stack gap-12 legal">
		<Hero
			title="Privacy — Pétanque Scan"
			tagline="Your camera images never leave your phone."
		/>

		<p class="updated">
			This policy covers <strong>the Pétanque Scan mobile app</strong>
			(formerly Pétanque Scanner, <code>com.raphbenpro.petanquear</code>), not the ludiven-studio.fr website, which has its
			<a href="/confidentialite/">own policy</a>. Last updated: 3 November 2026 (version 1.2.13: advertising moves from Google AdMob to Unity LevelPlay, with our own consent window; Google Firebase is removed; 10 free scans a day instead of 3).
		</p>
		<p class="updated">
			This is a courtesy translation. In case of discrepancy, the
			<a href="/petanque-scanner/confidentialite/" hreflang="fr">original French version</a> prevails.
		</p>

		<div class="summary">
			<p><strong>The essentials:</strong></p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Your camera images never leave your device.</strong> Boule detection is computed locally on the phone. No photo, no video and no image is sent to a server or stored permanently — including in photo mode, where the image taken when you press the shutter stays in RAM.</li>
				<li>There is <strong>no user account</strong>. We do not know your name, your email address or your location. Our only server is the one for usage statistics (see §5).</li>
				<li>Advertising starts <strong>only with your consent</strong>, requested at first launch. Without it, the app works just the same, without our partners' ads. You can change your mind at any time. Usage statistics, with no cookie and no identifier, do not depend on this choice (see §5).</li>
				<li>Buying <strong>Premium removes advertising</strong> and, in that case, the advertising SDK is not even started.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>1. Who is the data controller</h2>
			<p>Publisher of the app and data controller:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Company name: <strong>Ludiven Studio</strong></li>
				<li>Legal form: EURL (French single-member limited company) with share capital of €1,000</li>
				<li>Registration: 999&nbsp;253&nbsp;586 R.C.S. Vienne — SIRET 999&nbsp;253&nbsp;586&nbsp;00013</li>
				<li>Registered office: 1166 route de la Ranche, 38440 Châtonnay, France</li>
				<li>Publication director: Ludiven Studio</li>
				<li>Contact: <a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a></li>
			</ul>
			<p>See also the <a href="/mentions-legales/">legal notice</a> (in French).</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>2. The camera and augmented reality</h2>
			<p>
				Pétanque Scan needs camera access to work: it is the core of the app. It is important to understand
				exactly what is done with these images.
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Camera images are analysed <strong>in real time, entirely on your device</strong>, by an object detection model built into the app (no download, no network call for the analysis).</li>
				<li>Images are kept in RAM for the duration of the computation, then <strong>released immediately</strong>. They are not written to your gallery, to a file or to a persistent cache.</li>
				<li><strong>No image is transmitted</strong> to the publisher or to any third party, whatever your choice regarding advertising consent.</li>
				<li>Only the result of the computation (3D positions and distances) is used for display, and it disappears when you leave the scan.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				<strong>Photo mode.</strong> On phones that do not support augmented reality, the app automatically
				switches to a mode where you frame the pitch and then press a shutter button, instead of filming
				continuously. The principle stays the same: the image captured when you press the shutter is analysed
				<strong>in RAM only</strong>. It is not saved to a file, not added to your gallery and not transmitted; it
				is released as soon as you leave photo mode. In fact, the app asks for <strong>no permission to access your
				photos</strong>: only camera permission is required.
			</p>
			<p>
				As a result, use of the camera involves <strong>no collection of personal data</strong> by the publisher.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>3. Data processed</h2>
			<p>Here is the complete inventory of the processing carried out by the app.</p>
			<div class="table-scroll">
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Data</th>
							<th>Purpose</th>
							<th>Legal basis</th>
							<th>Recipient</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>Device advertising identifier (GAID on Android, IDFA on iOS if you allow tracking), other device identifiers, IP address, interactions with ads, technical information (see §4)</td>
							<td>Showing ads chosen according to your interests, measuring them, fighting fraud</td>
							<td>Consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR): without it, nothing starts</td>
							<td>Unity Technologies and its subsidiary ironSource (Unity LevelPlay, ironSource Ads, Unity Ads); through their auctions, other ad buyers (see §4)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>App usage events (see §5), together with: platform (Android or iOS), app and system version, device model, phone language, screen resolution</td>
							<td>Analytics: understanding which features are used and improving the app</td>
							<td>Legitimate interest (no cookie, no identifier, see §5)</td>
							<td>Umami, on our own server (Hetzner Online GmbH, Germany)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Your answer to the "Ads" window (accept or refuse), its date and the version of the text</td>
							<td>Remembering your decision, asking again after 6 months, being able to prove your choice</td>
							<td>Legal obligation</td>
							<td>Kept on your device only; Umami counts the yeses and noes, without any identifier (see §5)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Proof of purchase ("receipt") for Premium</td>
							<td>Unlocking and restoring your purchase</td>
							<td>Performance of the contract (Art. 6(1)(b))</td>
							<td>Apple or Google (app store)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Platform, price and app version when Premium is bought, without any identifier</td>
							<td>Telling the publisher about a sale</td>
							<td>Legitimate interest</td>
							<td>ntfy.sh (notification service), on a private channel</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Number of scans made today and today's date</td>
							<td>Running the limit of 10 free scans per day</td>
							<td>Performance of the contract</td>
							<td>No one: stays on the device</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>IP address, as for any web page</td>
							<td>Reading on our website the number of the latest version and, when it stands in for an ad, the Pétanque Meet video (see §8)</td>
							<td>Legitimate interest</td>
							<td>GitHub (our website's host)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Camera images</td>
							<td>Boule detection</td>
							<td>Performance of the contract</td>
							<td><strong>No one: local processing, no transmission</strong></td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p>
				The app does <strong>not</strong> collect: your name, your email address, your phone number, your
				contacts, your GPS location, your address book, your photos, or any identifier you may have entered. There
				is no account creation.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>4. Advertising and consent</h2>
			<p>
				The app is free and funded by an advertising banner, as well as by an optional video that you can
				choose to watch to recharge your free scans. Since version 1.2.13, ads are served by <strong>Unity
				LevelPlay</strong> with the <strong>ironSource Ads</strong> and <strong>Unity Ads</strong> networks
				(Unity Technologies and its subsidiary ironSource). Google no longer plays any part in the
				advertising or in your consent. Earlier versions, until they are updated, still use Google AdMob and
				its consent window (Google UMP).
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Your consent.</strong> At first launch, whatever your country, an "Ads" window asks whether
				you accept that our ad partners (Unity Ads and ironSource) use an identifier of your phone to choose
				the ads and measure how they perform. "Accept" and "Refuse" carry the same weight.
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>If you accept</strong>: Unity LevelPlay starts and shows the banner and the videos.</li>
				<li><strong>If you refuse</strong>: no advertising module starts. The app works just the same, without our partners' ads: in their place, a strip presents our other apps, Pétanque Meet or, on Android, Pétanque Game, and a short Pétanque Meet video also recharges your scans. This presentation sends nothing about you (see §8).</li>
				<li><strong>Your answer</strong>, its date and the version of the text stay on your phone. The app asks you again after 6 months, whether you accepted or refused, or sooner if our ad partners change.</li>
				<li><strong>On iOS</strong>, Apple's tracking permission (<em>App Tracking Transparency</em>) is only requested after an "Accept", and only serves advertising; without it, the iPhone's advertising identifier is not used.</li>
				<li><strong>Usage statistics</strong> (see §5) do not depend on your answer: they hold no advertising identifier, no cookie and no device identifier.</li>
				<li><strong>If you buy Premium</strong>: advertising disappears and the advertising module is no longer started.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				<strong>If you have accepted</strong>, to show ads, choose them, measure them and fight fraud, the
				ironSource and Unity Ads modules receive your phone's <strong>advertising identifier</strong> and
				other device identifiers, your <strong>IP address</strong> (which gives an approximate location, at
				city level), your interactions with the ads, how long you use the app, technical information
				(performance, crashes) and, according to Unity Ads, the purchases made in the app. Their auctions
				may pass the ad request on to other ad buyers.
			</p>
			<p>
				To learn more, and for ironSource's and Unity Ads' partners: <a
				href="https://unity.com/legal/game-player-and-app-user-privacy-policy" target="_blank"
				rel="noopener">Unity's privacy policy</a>, which covers Unity Ads, LevelPlay and ironSource.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>5. Analytics: the exact events</h2>
			<p>
				For transparency, here is the complete list of the events sent to <strong>Umami</strong>, a
				cookie-free statistics tool installed on our own server. They are sent whether you accept or refuse
				advertising: none contains data you have entered, any identifier, or the results of your
				measurements.
			</p>
			<p>
				Since version 1.2.13, Firebase Analytics (Google) receives nothing any more. Earlier versions, until
				they are updated, still send it these events if you had accepted.
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li><code>scan_started</code> — a scan starts</li>
				<li><code>scan_completed</code> — a scan completes, with the number of scans made that day</li>
				<li><code>scan_cancelled</code> — a scan is abandoned, with whether it counted for the day</li>
				<li><code>scan_blocked_quota</code> — a scan is refused because the daily limit has been reached</li>
				<li><code>welcome_choice</code> — the mode chosen on the welcome screen (augmented reality or photo)</li>
				<li><code>floor_confirmed</code> / <code>floor_rejected</code> — you confirm or reject the ground detection, with whether the scan starts over</li>
				<li><code>cochonet_redo</code> — you ask to search for the jack again</li>
				<li><code>ar_incompatible_shown</code> — your phone does not support augmented reality; you are shown this information</li>
				<li><code>camera_permission_denied</code> / <code>camera_settings_opened</code> / <code>camera_permission_recovered</code> — camera access is refused, you open the phone's settings, then access is granted</li>
				<li><code>photo_offer_shown</code> / <code>photo_offer_declined</code> — photo mode is offered to you, or you decline it</li>
				<li><code>photo_mode_entered</code> — photo mode starts, with the reason (automatic switch, offer accepted, or choice in the settings)</li>
				<li><code>photo_mode_exited</code> — photo mode is exited</li>
				<li><code>photo_shutter</code> — you take a photo, with an indication of whether the computation succeeded or failed</li>
				<li><code>photo_failed_…</code> — a photo's computation fails; the reason is in the event's name</li>
				<li><code>photo_retake</code> — you retake a photo</li>
				<li><code>photo_camera_unavailable</code> — the camera could not be opened</li>
				<li><code>settings_opened</code> — the settings screen is opened</li>
				<li><code>settings_action</code> — an action is triggered there: consent, privacy policy, terms of use, language, or purchase restore</li>
				<li><code>paywall_shown</code> / <code>paywall_dismissed</code> — the Premium offer screen is shown or closed, with the reason it was shown</li>
				<li><code>paywall_watch_ad</code> — you choose to watch a video to recharge your scans</li>
				<li><code>ad_reward_earned</code> — the ad was watched to the end and the scans are recharged</li>
				<li><code>ad_unavailable</code> — no ad was available to show</li>
				<li><code>meet_promo_shown</code> / <code>meet_promo_refill</code> / <code>meet_promo_closed</code> — the Pétanque Meet video is shown, recharges your scans, or is closed</li>
				<li><code>meet_store_opened</code> — you open Pétanque Meet's page in the store, from the strip or the video</li>
				<li><code>game_store_opened</code> — you open Pétanque Game's page in the store, from the strip</li>
				<li><code>premium_purchase_started</code> / <code>premium_purchase_success</code> / <code>premium_purchase_failed</code> — steps of a purchase, with the reason for failure where applicable</li>
				<li><code>premium_restore_success</code> — a previous purchase was restored</li>
				<li><code>premium_revoked</code> — the store no longer recognises a Premium (after a refund, for example)</li>
				<li><code>iap_receipt_invalid</code> — a proof of purchase could not be validated</li>
				<li><code>update_prompt</code> / <code>update_tapped</code> — an update is offered to you (recommended or required), or you tap the update button</li>
				<li><code>consent_accepted</code> / <code>consent_declined</code> — your consent choice</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				<strong>What Umami receives, precisely.</strong> Each event is sent to
				<code>stats.ludiven-studio.fr</code>, our server, with the following, and nothing more: the event
				name and its detail if any (for example the number of scans that day), a site identifier that
				belongs to us, the platform (<code>android</code> or <code>ios</code>), the app version, the system
				version, the phone model, the phone language and the screen resolution. <strong>No advertising
				identifier, no device number, no cookie and no persistent identifier</strong> is included. As with
				any request on the Internet, the server necessarily sees your IP address; our server does not store
				it: it is used only to infer the country, the region and the city, and to compute an anonymous
				fingerprint renewed every month, which can neither track you from one month to the next nor
				recognise you in another app.
			</p>
			<p>
				These statistics are linked to no one: we cannot find the ones that come from your phone. If you
				prefer that nothing is sent at all, use the app offline: scanning works without a network.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>6. Notifications</h2>
			<p>
				Since version 1.2.13, the app no longer receives notifications and no longer asks to allow them.
				Earlier versions, until they are updated, may still receive them through Firebase Cloud Messaging
				(Google) if you had accepted them; you can turn them off in your phone's settings.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>7. In-app purchases</h2>
			<p>
				The "Lifetime Premium" purchase is a one-off purchase handled <strong>entirely by Apple's App Store or by
				Google Play</strong>. We never see your payment details: no card number, no billing address, no identity.
				The app only receives a proof of purchase, verified locally, which is used to unlock the feature.
			</p>
			<p>
				With each purchase, the app also tells the publisher about the sale, with an alert sent to the
				<strong>ntfy.sh</strong> service on a private channel: the platform (Android or iOS), the price and
				the app version, without any identifier.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>8. What the app reads online</h2>
			<p>
				<strong>Our website.</strong> At launch, the app reads a small file on our website,
				ludiven-studio.fr, that gives the number of the latest version, to offer you an update. When the
				Pétanque Meet video stands in for an ad, it is read from our website too. Nothing is sent; as for
				any web page, the website's host (GitHub) sees your phone's IP address.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>9. What is stored on your device</h2>
			<p>
				Four pieces of information are stored locally, in the system's secure storage (Keychain on iOS,
				<em>EncryptedSharedPreferences</em> on Android):
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>the number of scans made today;</li>
				<li>the corresponding date, to know when to reset the counter;</li>
				<li>whether or not you own Premium;</li>
				<li>your consent choice.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Your answer to the "Ads" window, with its date and the version of the text, is also
				kept in the app's preferences, to know when to ask you again. If you have accepted advertising, the
				LevelPlay, ironSource and Unity Ads modules also keep their own data on the phone.
			</p>
			<p>
				This data is not synchronised to a server and is not backed up to the cloud by the app. Uninstalling the
				app erases it — with one exception: on iOS, the Premium flag may be kept by the Keychain, which is exactly
				what allows you to recover your purchase after reinstalling.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>10. Recipients and transfers outside the European Union</h2>
			<p>
				The only recipients of data are the providers listed below. We do not sell any data and share nothing
				with data brokers.
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Unity Technologies</strong> — advertising (Unity LevelPlay, Unity Ads), if you have accepted it.</li>
				<li><strong>ironSource</strong>, a subsidiary of Unity Technologies — advertising (ironSource Ads), if you have accepted it. The ironSource and Unity Ads auctions may pass the ad request on to other ad buyers (see §4).</li>
				<li><strong>Google Ireland Limited / Google LLC</strong> — only for versions earlier than 1.2.13, until they are updated: advertising (AdMob), consent management (UMP), analytics (Firebase Analytics), notifications (Firebase Cloud Messaging) and reference time (Firebase Realtime Database), if you had accepted them.</li>
				<li><strong>Hetzner Online GmbH</strong> (Germany) — hosting of our Umami analytics server. Versions of the app not yet updated still send this analytics data to <strong>Umami Software, Inc.</strong> (a US company), via the Umami Cloud service.</li>
				<li><strong>GitHub, Inc.</strong> — hosting of our website, read for the update offer and the Pétanque Meet video (see §8).</li>
				<li><strong>ntfy.sh</strong> — notification service that passes the sale alert on to us (see §7).</li>
				<li><strong>Apple Inc.</strong> and <strong>Google LLC</strong> — distribution of the app and processing of in-app purchases.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Some of this processing involves a transfer to the United States. These transfers are governed by the
				mechanisms provided for in Chapter V of the GDPR: standard contractual clauses and, for the providers
				concerned, certification under the <em>EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework</em>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>11. Retention periods</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Camera images</strong>: for the duration of the computation, in RAM only (a few milliseconds).</li>
				<li><strong>Analytics data — Firebase (versions earlier than 1.2.13)</strong>: kept by Firebase Analytics for <strong>14 months at most</strong>, according to the period set in the Firebase console. Aggregated reports (which cannot be linked to a device) may be kept longer.</li>
				<li><strong>Analytics data — Umami</strong>: kept as event statistics for <strong>24 months</strong> on our server, then erased; its backups are kept 14 days. Those Umami Cloud still receives from versions not yet updated are erased there after 6 months. This data is not linked to any device identifier and does not allow anyone's journey to be reconstructed.</li>
				<li><strong>Scan counter</strong>: reset every day.</li>
				<li><strong>Advertising data</strong>: according to the rules of Unity and ironSource.</li>
				<li><strong>Your answer about advertising</strong>: 6 months on the phone, then the app asks you again.</li>
				<li><strong>Premium flag</strong>: kept on the device until uninstallation (on iOS, the Keychain may keep it, see §9).</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>12. Your rights</h2>
			<p>
				Under the GDPR, you have the right of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and
				portability, as well as the right to withdraw your consent at any time.
			</p>
			<p><strong>In practice:</strong></p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Withdraw or change your consent</strong>: tap "Manage ad consent" in the app's settings: the "Ads" window comes back. If you refuse, our partners' advertising stops at once. Tracking on iOS can also be turned off in Settings › Privacy &amp; Security › Tracking.</li>
				<li><strong>Erase local data</strong>: uninstall the app, or clear its data from the phone's settings.</li>
				<li><strong>Reset your advertising identifier</strong>: Android → Settings › Google › Ads; iOS → Settings › Privacy &amp; Security › Tracking.</li>
				<li><strong>Exercise your rights with us</strong>: write to <a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>. We reply within one month. Please note that, as there is no user account or identifier allowing us to recognise you, it is materially impossible for us to find data concerning "you" in our statistics: they are aggregated and not linked to an identifiable person on our side.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				If you believe your rights are not being respected, you can lodge a complaint with the French data
				protection authority, the CNIL (<a href="https://www.cnil.fr" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.cnil.fr</a>),
				3 place de Fontenoy, TSA 80715, 75334 Paris Cedex 07.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>13. Children</h2>
			<p>
				The app is not intended for children and is not designed as a service aimed at minors. It is not declared
				as such to the app stores and does not knowingly target under-16s. If you hold parental authority and
				notice that a child has used the app, contact us.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>14. Security</h2>
			<p>
				Data stored locally is kept using the secure storage mechanisms provided by the operating system. All network exchanges are encrypted (HTTPS/TLS). As there is no application server of Pétanque
				Scan's own, the exposure surface is limited to the providers listed in §10.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>15. Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>
				This policy may change, in particular if the app gains new features. The date of the last update appears
				at the top of the page. In the event of a substantial change affecting your rights, you will be asked for
				new consent in the app.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>16. Contact</h2>
			<p>
				For any question about this policy:
				<a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>.
			</p>
			<p>See also the <a href="/en/petanque-scanner/cgu/">app's terms of use</a>.</p>
		</section>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.legal {
		max-width: 68ch;
		margin-inline: auto;
		color: var(--gray-200);
		font-size: var(--text-md);
		line-height: 1.6;
	}
	.legal h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}
	.legal ul {
		padding-left: 1.2rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.35rem;
	}
	.legal a {
		color: var(--accent-regular);
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
	}
	.legal a:hover,
	.legal a:focus {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}
	.updated {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--gray-300);
